-- title:
--   Uniqueness of A-points through a crossing on a crossing chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, and the hypothesis `hj` that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for $X_H$ over the base ring `R p`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R p \to A$ compatible with $R p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $R p \to O$, whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, equipped with $toκ : O \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, $jO : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $ιA : O \to A$ satisfying the stated compatibilities with $\rho$, the residue map of $A$ and the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` attached to $\mathfrak{X}$, and write $x_n$ for its image in $X_O :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the base change of the model to $O$, under the first projection followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and by `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO toκ htoκ`. Let $e \ge 1$, let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X_O$ containing $x_n$, and let $f : U \to \mathrm{Spec}\,\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)\bigr)$ be a morphism over $\mathrm{Spec}\,O$ (hypothesis `hover`). Assume: a point $y$ of $U$ has both coordinates `CrossingQuotient.U (((p : ℕ) : O) ^ e)` and `CrossingQuotient.V (((p : ℕ) : O) ^ e)` in the prime $f(y)$ exactly when $y$ lies over $x_n$; at every such $y$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and induces an isomorphism of residue fields, and $y$ has an open neighbourhood $V$ in $U$ with $V \hookrightarrow U$ followed by $f$ étale; and the two branches of the crossing match the two components, in the sense that the second coordinate lies in $f(y)$ if and only if $y$ lies over the image of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` composed with `bcMap`, and the first coordinate lies in $f(y)$ if and only if $y$ lies over the image of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` composed with `bcMap`. Then any two morphisms $s, s' : \mathrm{Spec}\,A \to U$ whose composites to $\mathrm{Spec}\,O$ equal $\mathrm{Spec}(ιA)$, whose closed points both map to $x_n$ in $X_O$, and which satisfy $s$ followed by $f$ equals $s'$ followed by $f$, are equal.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the statement that the annulus around a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport style model of $X_H$ at $p$ is parametrised injectively by the local crossing chart $uv = p^e$: two $A$-valued points through the crossing with the same image under the chart coincide. It is used in the construction of that annulus parametrisation, in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_annulus_mem_dom_iff_and_param_eq_read_chart_and_modulus_eq_pow_of_chart_of_residue_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_annulus_mem_dom_iff_and_param_eq_read_chart_and_modulus_eq_pow_of_chart_of_residue_surjective).
